WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:09.090
Light travels in straight lines.
It will not bend round a corner.

2
00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:12.608
You see a book when light
bounces off it into your eye.

3
00:00:13.108 --> 00:00:16.776
Shine a torch through dusty
air. The beam is dead straight.

4
00:00:16.996 --> 00:00:21.130
Sunlight through a gap in the
clouds comes down in straight lines.

5
00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:25.204
You cannot see round a corner.
Light will not bend round it.

6
00:00:25.424 --> 00:00:29.511
The light from behind the corner
travels straight, and misses your eye.

7
00:00:29.731 --> 00:00:33.632
Scientists draw light as rays:
straight lines with arrows.

8
00:00:34.132 --> 00:00:38.961
When light hits a surface, some of
it bounces off. That is reflection.

9
00:00:39.181 --> 00:00:42.711
A mirror reflects neatly,
in one new straight line.

10
00:00:42.931 --> 00:00:47.064
A book reflects roughly, scattering
the light in every direction.

11
00:00:47.284 --> 00:00:51.649
Pale and shiny surfaces reflect
most of the light that hits them.

12
00:00:51.869 --> 00:00:55.538
Dark surfaces soak most of
it up, so they look dark.

13
00:00:56.038 --> 00:00:59.800
A torch, a mirror and an
eye. Watch what the ray does.

14
00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:04.246
Predict first. Will the ray
bounce, stop dead, or curve round?

15
00:01:04.466 --> 00:01:09.110
Turn the mirror. It bounces off in a
new straight line, as you predicted.

16
00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:13.927
At the right angle the ray reaches
the eye, and you see the torch.

17
00:01:14.147 --> 00:01:18.606
Put a book in the way. It blocks the
ray, so the mirror shows no torch.

18
00:01:19.106 --> 00:01:24.260
Only a light source makes light. You
see everything else by reflection.

19
00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:28.010
The lamp shines on the book.
The book is not a source.

20
00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:32.502
It reflects some of that light off
its surface, in every direction.

21
00:01:32.722 --> 00:01:36.763
A little of it travels straight
into your eye. Now you see the book.

22
00:01:36.983 --> 00:01:40.837
Switch the lamp off. Nothing
reflects, so you see nothing at all.

23
00:01:41.057 --> 00:01:47.187
The Sun, a lamp and a candle make light.
The Moon and a mirror only reflect.

24
00:01:47.687 --> 00:01:51.449
For a thousand years people
believed the eye sent out beams.

25
00:01:51.669 --> 00:01:55.198
But if that were true, why
can nobody see in a dark room?

26
00:01:55.418 --> 00:01:59.459
Ibn al-Haytham built dark rooms
with tiny holes and tested it.

27
00:01:59.679 --> 00:02:05.298
He showed light comes into the eye, not out
of it. Evidence changed what everyone knew.

28
00:02:05.798 --> 00:02:10.581
Now draw it all: the light source,
the ray, the mirror and the eye.

29
00:02:10.801 --> 00:02:14.238
The source first. Every
ray starts at the torch.

30
00:02:14.458 --> 00:02:19.520
A ruler line to the mirror, with an
arrow pointing away from the torch.

31
00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:24.244
Then a second straight line into
the eye. That is your ray diagram.

32
00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:29.760
Light travels in straight lines,
and we draw it as rays with arrows.

33
00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:34.949
Light reflects off surfaces: neatly
off a mirror, roughly off a book.

34
00:02:35.169 --> 00:02:39.581
You see a thing when light from a
source bounces off it into your eye.

35
00:02:39.801 --> 00:02:44.863
Evidence from enquiry changed the
old idea. That is how science works.
